  annotation "note_1771590290946_0", anchor: "scored gouges where Qingfu'spire's guard had dragged equipment during the seizure", text: "The chronicler treats these as navigational landmarks — fourteen steps, left at the gouges, right at the gallery. But the Berg's ice preserves literal impressions. These scored marks are not scenery. They are testimony, frozen into the structure, and they will outlast everyone who made them and everyone who walks past them. Qing reads them with her feet without knowing she is reading.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771590290946_1", anchor: "the long white mark on her left flipper, souvenir of a war that had ended and a choice that hadn't", text: "Left flipper. I have read this line more times than the work required. A scar there changes how you carry things, how you grip, how you gesture without thinking. She keeps hers loose. I keep mine still. The same lesson.", type: :tangent, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771590290946_2", anchor: "The corruption's spreading, you know. From Promenade Hei.", text: "Promenade Ward is Qingfu'spire's sovereign territory — the seat of their governance. If corruption is spreading from within their administrative center, the schism did not merely fracture political authority; it fractured the maintenance of sanctified zones. The Pinnacle's splinter drew away the very workers who would have caught this early. Neither faction will admit that the other's absence made them weaker. The ice will record it regardless.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771590290946_3", anchor: "Qing sat in the stillness and watched the light go wrong", text: "During each Long Dark, some penguins simply walk out onto the ice. The compulsion seizes those who have lost much. Every impression I have catalogued begins like this — not with despair but with completion. The task done. The tea finished. The stillness settling into place like a key turning. The chronicler does not name what this is. Perhaps it is nothing. Perhaps she stays. I note only that the account ends here, and that we are not told what morning comes next.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771590290946_4", anchor: "Seventeen tokens no one visited. She knew the count without looking.", text: "She knew it without looking because seventeen is not a count. It is a liturgy. I have flagged this number before and will again.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
